# pyron COSMO DISRUPTION — the HARD repro attempt (14z-75).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. 14z-74 "fixed" a maintainer-reported Cosmo crash with a
# one-word repoint that 14z-75 proved (a) corrupts legacy for every character
# and (b) is BIT-IDENTICAL for Pyron on replay 71 — i.e. it never affected the
# move at all. Before building any replacement, the crash has to be
# REPRODUCED. Replay 71 fires the EX exactly ONCE (attempt 1 spends no stock;
# only attempt 2 does, ~f3900) and neither build resets, so it is too weak to
# support a "no crash" claim in either direction.
#
# This rig fires the EX repeatedly with both button pairs, keeping the meter
# topped up so no attempt is silently downgraded (the standing trap: with an
# empty meter the pair becomes a single button and NOTHING fires).
#
# RUN WITH (stocks re-poked throughout — the move spends one each time):
#   POKES="1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;\
#          3300:ff8509:09;3700:ff8509:09;4100:ff8509:09;4500:ff8509:09;\
#          4900:ff8509:09;5300:ff8509:09;5700:ff8509:09;6100:ff8509:09;\
#          6500:ff8509:09;6900:ff8509:09;7300:ff8509:09;7700:ff8509:09"
#
# VERDICT: a watchdog reset is NOT a 68k exception, so the crash guard cannot
# see it (14z-74 established this). Judge by whether the MATCH SURVIVES —
# fighter block + match state still live at the end — or by snapshots.
300-305 sys=C1
800-803 sys=S1
1700-1702 p1=1
# 12 attempts, alternating 2K (45) and 2P (12), every 400 frames from 3400.
3400-3402 p1=L
